|description={{en|1=Rules covering life membership to the library exchangeable at any library station in the United States, Canada, or Great Britain are provided for the library service. A description of exchange fees charged weekly, and a penny a day when overdue, capped at 25 cents, with a requirement to exchange books four times a month. Books are stored in a Tabard Inn cloth case. Instructions for discontinuing service allow books to be turned in for an out-of-service check that can be exchanged for a book later. Purchase of another book allows membership to continue when books are lost. A table is listed at the bottom to log the activity of the books as they are checked out and returned. The home office of The Tabard Inn Library is listed at Chestnut Street in Philadelphia, PA}}
